  message: "Pass 36 (continuing 06022026_1622) entrypoint kind flag-gating reframing.\n\nF36.D1 (entrypoint kind vocabulary is flag-conditional): pass-30 F30.4 noted '4 of 10 documented entrypoint kinds ABSENT from substrate: cli_command, background_task, websocket_handler, connectivity_based'. Pass-36 finds cli_command IS detectable but flag-gated behind --include-docs: adds 4 cli_command EPs to root (104→108) and 3 to tracker (15→18). Pass-30 F30.4's framing should narrow to 'absent from DEFAULT substrate'; the 10-kind documented vocabulary is partially flag-gated. Same family as F34.A2/F35.A2 feature-flag-gating: the substrate vocabulary expansion is tied to specific flag activation. Remaining 3 truly-absent kinds (background_task, websocket_handler, connectivity_based) may also be flag-gated rather than producer-missing — worth a future probe sweep across --frameworks all / --max-tier / --first-party-only / --no-handler-slices to identify whose flag activates each kind."  # 94ed
